2. HTTP Methods

HTTP methods tell the web server what action the client wants to perform.

GET

Used to retrieve data from a server.

Examples:

- HTML page
- Image
- Other resources

GET → Retrieve

POST

Used to send/submit data to a server.

Examples:

- Submit a form
- Upload data

POST → Submit data

PUT

Used to create or replace/update a resource at a specified location.

PUT → Create / Replace

DELETE

Used to request deletion of a specified resource.

DELETE → Delete

Quick Revision

GET     → Retrieve
POST    → Submit
PUT     → Create / Replace
DELETE  → Delete

