3. FTP — File Transfer Protocol

FTP is used to transfer files between a client and a server.

Default Port

FTP → TCP 21

Port 21 is used for the FTP control connection. File transfers use a separate data connection.

Important FTP Commands

Command| Purpose
"USER"| Provides the username
"PASS"| Provides the password
"RETR"| Retrieves/downloads a file
"STOR"| Uploads/stores a file

Examples

USER anonymous
PASS

Anonymous FTP may allow access without a normal user account, depending on the server configuration.

---

Basic FTP Client Workflow

ftp <server-ip>

After connecting:

USER anonymous
PASS
ls
get flag.txt
quit

After returning to the normal shell, a downloaded text file can be viewed with:

cat flag.txt

«"ascii" is an FTP transfer mode used for text files. It is not required for every FTP download.»

