4. SMTP — Simple Mail Transfer Protocol

SMTP is used for sending email and transferring mail between mail servers.

Default Port

SMTP → TCP 25

Important SMTP Commands

Command| Purpose
"HELO"| Initiates an SMTP session
"EHLO"| Extended version of "HELO"
"MAIL FROM:"| Specifies the sender
"RCPT TO:"| Specifies the recipient
"DATA"| Begins the email message
"."| On a line by itself, indicates the end of the message

Basic Flow

HELO / EHLO
      ↓
MAIL FROM:
      ↓
RCPT TO:
      ↓
DATA
      ↓
Email content
      ↓
.

The single "." on its own line tells the SMTP server that the message content has ended.

