5. POP3 — Post Office Protocol Version 3

POP3 is used to retrieve email from a mail server.

Default Port

POP3 → TCP 110

Important POP3 Commands

Command| Purpose
"USER <username>"| Identifies the user
"PASS <password>"| Provides the password
"STAT"| Shows number of messages and total size
"LIST"| Lists messages and their sizes
"RETR <number>"| Retrieves a specific message
"DELE <number>"| Marks a message for deletion
"QUIT"| Ends the session and applies pending changes

Basic POP3 Workflow

Connect
  ↓
USER
  ↓
PASS
  ↓
STAT
  ↓
LIST
  ↓
RETR <message_number>
  ↓
QUIT

Telnet Example

A basic way to interact with a POP3 service in a lab environment:

telnet <server-ip> 110

Then:

USER <username>
PASS <password>
STAT
LIST
RETR <message_number>
QUIT

«The exact commands and credentials depend on the lab environment. Don't use credentials against systems you don't have permission to access.»

